
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Native regression checks (Zig C++ compiler required):
    python test/run_native.py --compiler <path-to-zig>

These compile the production USB parser and phase estimator with fake I/O,
exercise partial/malformed/max-size packets and USB backpressure, stress DMA
buffer ownership with delayed consumers, and validate PWM periods over 1-100 kHz.
The ZCD checks include REF loss, timer rollover and long capture windows.

Firmware build and ST-Link programming:
    pio run
    pio run --target upload

On hardware, verify the ADC block counter continues increasing (about 732/s),
no ADC/DMA error is set, the selected capture source matches TIM2 enable state,
and the host can still read configuration/status and dual-channel snapshots.

USB smoke checks after upload (pyserial required, sonication remains off):
    python test/hardware_usb_smoke.py --port COM20

Checks firmware version, maximum-size frames, recovery after truncation, and
both 240-sample ADC waveform packets. Close the DAQ connection before running.
